# A complaint, answered (IDEAS I20 a; QUESTIONS Q28 and Q29, 5; board 0.6; docs/features/F68-the-desktop-is-what-is-left-over.md).
# Story: two windows, side by side, are two halves of the screen, by two docks or by Arrange Windows. No column is left for the Desktop.
open Safari
open Notes
dock 101 left
expect size 101 702x851
dock 102 right
expect still 101
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 702x851
expect at 102 726 37
expect size 102 702x851
float-all
arrange
expect count docked 2
expect size 101 702x851
expect size 102 702x851
# The Desktop can still be gone to.
desktop
expect camera desktop
back
# Whoever is left alone stays as it is: what is freed is left over, where it was freed.
close 101
expect still 102
expect at 102 726 37
expect size 102 702x851
# Arrange Windows with three to six windows: no column, and no gap for one. The last column ends where the display's margin begins.
open Mail
open Terminal
arrange
expect count docked 3
expect above 103 104
expect size 102 702x851
expect at 102 726 37
open Music
arrange
expect above 105 102
expect size 102 702x419
expect at 102 726 469
open Maps
open Preview
arrange
expect count docked 6
expect size 103 464x420
expect at 103 12 37
expect size 102 464x419
expect at 102 964 469
# The old thirds by the setting.
float-all
set desktopColumn true
dock 102 left
dock 103 right
expect size 102 464x851
expect size 103 464x851
expect at 103 964 37
